# A recorded code test removes the small-gap preparation bottleneck

Fix the exact completed Wilson-Maxwell source and every inherited charge,
reference, native constituent, physical Gauss isometry and clock. Its only
family parameter here is the photon occupation cap K>=3. The parent
`native_wilson_maxwell_ground_refinement` establishes a unique active physical
ground in its code P, uniformly in K, and a mathematical five-oscillator
comparison. This proof changes the apparatus setting only. It does not
replace a parent receipt or claim that a generic passive repair protocol
implements these exact finite matrix controls.

## Record the sector before comparing energies

On one actual native trial the parent's exact decomposition is

`P rho_trial P = p_code |0><0|`, `p_code>=p0^32`.

Here |0> is the declared free filled sea and photon vacuum. The retained
preparation references are not discarded. A pure active marginal factors
from its environment upon this recorded admission. Run four independent
trials and implement the four commuting binary tests {P,I-P}. Keep every
one of the 16 flag strings and all rejected source states. The all-code
branch has probability at least p_code^4 and has active input |0>^tensor4.
Every other branch runs the same number of declared no-op slots. There
is no retry or unrecorded conditional ensemble.

The actual Hamiltonian commutes with P. Every subsequent energy agreement
operation on the admitted branch therefore stays in the code. The small
gap to native complementary states cannot enter that operation. The parent
already proves that its code ground is the full active physical ground;
this observation does not change that proof or its very small full gap.

## Center the instrument, not the physical Hamiltonian

Use the known source baseline `E_base=32 E_g+m(3+sqrt(6))` and set

`h=(H-E_base)/m`, `C=(I-i h)(I+i h)^-1` on the admitted code.

Extend C by identity on the physical code complement and the outer
constraint-failure sector. These blocks never enter an admitted filter,
and this extension gives the complete-carrier norm comparison below.

This defines an apparatus coefficient. The autonomous source, work account
and clock retain H with its full raw baseline. E_base is known from the
native Hamiltonian and photon zero points. It is not the unknown interacting
ground energy, and no interacting eigenvector enters the controller.

The parent gives the ground eigenvalue x and code gap gamma with

`10^-6<=x<=mu_U<0.000100230944`, `gamma>1.3284353259`.

For an excited eigenvalue x+delta, delta>=gamma, the Cayley chord is

`2 delta/sqrt[(1+x^2)(1+(x+delta)^2)]`.

For x>=0 it is increasing in delta: the derivative of its logarithm is
`[1+x(x+delta)]/[delta(1+(x+delta)^2)]>0`. At fixed delta it decreases
with x. Hence the minimum is bounded by substituting x=mu_U,delta=gamma.
Exact rational arithmetic verifies

`4 gamma^2 > (3/2)^2 (1+mu_U^2)(1+(mu_U+gamma)^2)`.

The separation is therefore strictly greater than 3/2 even though code
excited energies grow without bound in the comparison. No norm bound on
all excited energies, and no small full physical gap, is required.

For M=4096, use the uniform pointer, controlled powers of C tensor C^dagger,
inverse uniform preparation and measurement of every pointer state. Pointer
zero has Kraus operator `M^-1 sum_(j=0)^(M-1) (C tensor C^dagger)^j`.
Its mixed ground/excited amplitude is at most

`epsilon=2/[(3/2)M]=1/3072`.

All 4096 pointer outcomes are retained. Equal ground energies pass with
amplitude one. This construction does not assume that all excited pairs
are separated; they may pass, and are included in the following bound.

## Complete tree and stationary occupation

Let kappa be the parent's uniform ground-angle upper bound and set
`r0=kappa^2`. After code admission the active free vacuum has ground
probability at least `1/(1+r0)`. The orthogonal ground/ground, mixed and
excited/excited sectors give, for each two-copy filter,

`r_(j+1)<=r_j^2+2 epsilon^2 r_j`.

Use two independent first-level filters and one final filter. The original
attempt probability of all four admissions and all three zero outcomes is
at least

`q=p_code^4 (1+r0)^-4 (1+r1)^-2`.

The final main-source ground fidelity is at least F=1/(1+r2). Every partner,
reference and previous pointer remains present; its purification comparison
error is at most `eta=sqrt(2-2sqrt(F))`. Failed ancestor flags control no-op
descendant slots. The final detector also retains every failure flag.

For the parent's free-frame T111 count projector, its independently proved
ground amplitude a_G yields original-attempt probability

`Pr(all admissions, all filters pass, T111)>=q (a_G-eta)^2>0`.

The count is a stationary dressed-ground occupation in a specified free
frame. It is not emitted radiation, a particle rest mass or a scattering
state. Every final count and complementary outcome remains in the law.

For an initial positive-record witness a smaller complete setting suffices:
two source trials, two code flags, one energy-agreement filter with M=64,
and the complete count. Substitute epsilon=1/48 into the first recurrence.
The original all-pass probability exceeds .99966239936, purification error
is below .000417094261, and original T111 probability exceeds 6.4978e-8.
This is a separate four-slot instrument with weaker ground accuracy. It
retains every failure and requires neither four copies nor a 4096-state
pointer. The claim is sufficiency, not optimality of the 64-state choice.

## Quantitative fixed-alphabet cap comparison

Use the parent's common Fock comparison extension: finite link exponentials
are extended by identity beyond the cap. On the code h_K=a+b_K, with a
independent of K, a>=2N and ||b_K||<=48. The positive Coulomb and reference
terms are in a. The exact zero-phase-removed matter lower bound in the
parent is needed here; using a nonpositive arbitrary split would invalidate
the estimate. The link displacement lemma gives for L=floor(K/2),n=K+1

`||(b_K-b_inf) P_(<=L)||<=48/n^2`, `||b_K-b_inf||<=96`.

Its guards K>=7 and `6 r sqrt(n)/(n-L)<=1/16` are explicitly checked.
With R_h=(h+i)^-1 and R_a=(a+i)^-1, self-adjointness gives ||R_h||<=1 and

`R_h=R_a(I-b R_h)`, `||I-b R_h||<=49`.

Since a preserves photon number and a>=2N,
`||R_a P_(>L)||<=1/[2(L+1)]<=1/n`, and ||R_a||<=1. Resolvent identity
and the adjoint factorization `C^dagger=-I+2i(h+i)^-1` give
`||C_K-C_inf||=2||R_K-R_inf||`, hence

`||C_K-C_inf||<=98[48/n^2+96/n]<10000/n`.

This uses neither a Neumann-series smallness assumption on b nor a cutoff-
dependent pointer. The code admission is exact and identical under the
comparison embedding, including its entire rejected branches. Initial
trials have photon vacuum and agree exactly for every K. There is no
ground-state replacement error at the input.

The two-copy comparison differs by at most twice this Cayley bound.
Telescoping controlled powers up to M-1 bounds each complete filter
isometry by `2(M-1)d_C`. Three filters, including adaptive no-op branches,
therefore have complete-history error at most `6(M-1)d_C`.
The errors concern normalized original trials and their full classical/
quantum environment before any conditioning. Total variation of any
subsequent complete record law is bounded by the same vector norm bound.

Unlike the parent setting, the declared controls below cancel background
evolution during each slot. There are no additional free-evolution factors
to telescope. The count projectors agree on the shared occupation basis;
the comparison's occupation>K counts can be binned into an explicit overflow
label. Finite K has zero such probability. Arbitrarily many comparison
count labels may instead be retained by padding the finite law with zeroes.

For two additional bounded E/B tests, the complete energy filters preserve
each source's energy on average, including every pointer outcome. Conditional
only on the initial all-code flags the mean dimensionless energy is <=mu_U.
The parent form inequality `h>=0.9 H0-b`, H0>=2N, gives

`<N><=(mu_U+b)/1.8`.

On admission-failure branches the tests are no-ops. No normalization by a
later filter success is used in this estimate. A displacement of radius r
increases ||sqrt(N) psi|| by at most r on the infinite comparison. Before
either test use the conservative accumulated radius
`R=(sqrt(1/2)+sqrt(2))/64`. Its single-test discrepancy is at most

`n^-2+2(sqrt(<N>)+R)/sqrt(L+1)`.

At K=2^64 the complete preparation, flags and two-test law differs from
the fixed-cube comparison by less than 10^-8. Exact outward numbers are in
results.json. This is a photon-cap comparison, not a spatial, ultraviolet
or relativistic continuum limit.

## One clock and explicit apparatus costs

There are six duration-one slots on every branch: trial preparation, joint
code admission, three filters and final complete readout. Each chosen
finite unitary completion U is implemented by the constant control
`i Log U-H_copies` with the principal Hermitian logarithm. Background
cancellation is an explicitly supplied operation. The autonomous source
H is unchanged between interventions; it is not claimed to generate these
controls itself. All charge-compensating references remain in H_copies.

Using the parent's full raw finite bound B_raw(K), each control has norm
at most `4 B_raw(K)+pi`. Six on/off pulses have gross switching-work bound
`12[4 B_raw(K)+pi]`. The complete final capacity in nats is

`4[32(256ln2+8ln5+24ln119+ln(2^31+1))+7ln9+ln65`
`  +ln binom(K+5,5)] +4ln2+3ln4096+ln[290(K+1)+1]`.

The four extra bits retain every code-admission flag. The resource bound
includes all native trials, references, photon carriers and output pointers,
but excludes controller coefficient/synthesis workspace. No huge matrix is
claimed to have been enumerated and no efficient local compilation is proved.
Any physical implementation error must be bounded for the whole instrument
and charged to the original-attempt probability before conditioning.

For the smaller two-copy setting, replace four copies by two, four admission
bits by two, three pointers by one 64-state pointer, and six pulses by four.
Its complete filter-isometry error is `2(64-1)d_C`; the same two-field tail
estimate applies. At K=2^64 its entire local record error is still below
10^-8. Each control has norm at most `2B_raw(K)+pi` and gross switching work
at most `8[2B_raw(K)+pi]`. These resource differences are not hidden by
conditioning on the smaller setting's accepted events.
